      "name": "Guess who is coming to dinner",
      "sort": 100000,
      "type": "action",
      "folder": null,
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p data-visibility=\"gm\"><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature enters the top 15 feet of the deck of Area B8.</p>\n<p><strong>Effect&nbsp;</strong> A dwarven man (recognizable as the same one from the haunt in area B5) staggers out of the snow. His eyes are wild with fear, his clothes in tatters and blood drips from several cuts on his exposed flesh. When he sees he PCs, he cries out, <em><strong>\"Run! Run for your lives! They're going to eat you!\"</strong></em> With that, the dwarf flees into the snow.</p>\n<p>All PCs in the area are affected by a @Compendium[pf2e.spells-srd.4koZzrnMXhhosn0D]{Fear} spell with a @Check[type:will|dc:34]&nbsp;save. Anyone critcally failing the save and who race blindly into the snow in this manner have a flat 50% chance of running off the edge of the cliff, in which case they will fall 60 feet to the ground below.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"
        },
